A_647 - Cavities aren't caused by sugar, but by meat, specifically by putrefying bacteria that rise from the stomach. If you think about it, it's well known that saliva helps digest sugars, so it's unlikely that sugars are the cause. Furthermore, I've personally found that brushing your teeth isn't necessary if you don't eat meat, and I can confirm that I haven't had any cavities even after more than 15 consecutive years of not brushing my teeth. I even made a TikTok video about this.